<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Jobbliggaren.Migrate's testable decision surface, as a library rather than as statements
    inside a console Exe's top-level program. The Phase A privilege model (ADR 0034) was the
    first resident; the schema-ahead gate (#1236) is the second. What they share is the
    extraction rule (#1232): logic that only exists as awaits in a top-level Program is
    unreachable from every test assembly.

    WHY IT IS ITS OWN PROJECT AND NOT `InternalsVisibleTo` ON `Jobbliggaren.Migrate`.
    Four assemblies need this model: `Jobbliggaren.Migrate` executes it,
    `Jobbliggaren.Migrate.UnitTests` pins it, and `Jobbliggaren.Api.IntegrationTests` and
    `Jobbliggaren.Worker.IntegrationTests` provision a test database with it so their oracles run
    under the same privilege posture production does (#1232, #197). IVT is the escape hatch for a
    test peeking at internals; it is not the mechanism for four assemblies sharing a model, and
    `Jobbliggaren.Migrate`
    is a composition root (CLAUDE.md §2.1) rather than a library to reference.

    There is also a concrete compile hazard on the IVT route. Both `Jobbliggaren.Api` and
    `Jobbliggaren.Migrate` use top-level statements, so both generate a `Program` type in the
    global namespace. `Jobbliggaren.Api.IntegrationTests` names `WebApplicationFactory<Program>`
    unqualified in 11 files; granting it IVT to Migrate would make a second `Program`
    accessible there, which is CS0433. Neither existing consumer exercises that combination —
    `Migrate.UnitTests` does not reference Api, and `Architecture.Tests` references both but
    holds no IVT.

    NO PACKAGE REFERENCES ON PURPOSE. These types emit SQL text or decide over string sets;
    they never execute anything. Npgsql and EF stay in `Jobbliggaren.Migrate`, which owns
    connections and logging.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Jobbliggaren.Migrate</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Jobbliggaren.Migrate.Provisioning</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
